# oracle: pair_style sw with the multi-element CdTeZnSeHgS0.sw file (Cd Te Zn, three types), displaced lattice, velocities from atom-style variables, 50 steps of nve
# oracle-potentials: CdTeZnSeHgS0.sw
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 3.9e-13, atoms 6.5e-14.
# The three-body term takes the parameters of the (center, j, k) entry with j before k in native's full-list neighbour order (npair_bin.cpp: the stencil, then each bin chain); this file gives different parameters to orders such as Te Te Zn and Te Zn Te.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         diamond 5.6
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      3 box
create_atoms    1 box
group         t2 id 2:216:3
set             group t2 type 2
group         t3 id 3:216:3
set             group t3 type 3
mass            1 112.41
mass            2 127.6
mass            3 65.38
variable        dx atom 0.05*sin(1.3*x+0.7*y)
variable        dy atom 0.05*cos(0.9*y-0.4*z)
variable        dz atom 0.05*sin(1.1*z+0.5*x)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.01*sin(id)
variable        vy atom 0.01*cos(2*id)
variable        vz atom 0.01*sin(3*id)
pair_style sw
pair_coeff * * CdTeZnSeHgS0.sw Cd Te Zn
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ke press pxx pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          10
run             50
